<item>
            <title>[ITEP-87225] Multi-Object, Multi-View Tracking Metrics and Tooling, Phase 1</title>
                <link>https://jira.devtools.intel.com/browse/ITEP-87225</link>
                <project id="99912" key="ITEP">EdgeSW</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Multi-object, multi-view (or multi-camera) tracking is a critical workload, and the system must adopt modern metrics and measure against popular new datasets.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Current metrics used in testing are:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;MSE: mean-squared error&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;MSOCE: mean-squared object count error&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;IDC: ID change error&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Based on &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/open-edge-platform/scenescape/blob/main/docs/adr/0009-tracking-evaluation.md&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;ADR 9: Tracking Evaluation Strategy&lt;/a&gt;, implement Phase 1: Close critical gaps with minimal effort.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Use an offline black-box evaluation harness for the scene controller.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Integrate an established evaluation toolkit (e.g., TrackEval) and implement adapters for SceneScape I/O formats.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Add localization (position) metrics evaluation (e.g., MOTP, LocA) with TrackEval to complement existing system tests.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Add basic trajectory smoothness metrics to detect jitter regressions (e.g., RMS jerk, acceleration variance).&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Extend Basic Acceptance Tests with threshold-based evaluation of the new metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Core requirements:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The evaluation toolkit must operate in metric coordinate space (meters in x, y, and z), and any dataset used must provide compatible ground truth.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The evaluation toolkit must also account for standard time such that velocity and related measurements can be reported in meters per second (m/s) units. Timing based on frame numbers alone is not acceptable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;The system must be extensible to account for varying object shapes as well as object orientation (e.g. cuboid measurement with orientation of a vehicle in a parking slot, or a cylindrical representation of a person&#8217;s location)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&apos;table-wrap&apos;&gt;
